  "_notes": "Sources: Kodi core ids/extensions from each game.libretro.* addon.xml in the tv.kodi.Kodi flatpak build and the LibreELEC add-on repository (ARMv8/aarch64 and Generic/x86_64); cores are offered only when Kodi reports them installed or installable, so a core missing on one build is harmless; slugs validated against RomM backend/utils/platform_slugs.py (UniversalPlatformSlug); aliases from RomM alembic 0046_migrate_platform_slugs.py OLD_SLUGS_TO_NEW_MAP, backend/utils/platform_aliases.py PLATFORM_FS_ALIASES (Batocera/RetroBat/ES-DE folder names), Grout bios/data/platform_cores.json fs_slugs and common IGDB-era slugs. Core preference was cross-checked against Grout platform_cores.json and RomM frontend _EJS_CORES_MAP. Ordering is best-first for a TV box: accuracy and compatibility over speed (beetle-psx > swanstation > pcsx-rearmed; beetle-saturn > yabasanshiro > yabause; mesen-s > supafaust > beetle-bsnes as no snes9x core exists in Kodi; mesen > nestopia > fceumm > quicknes; mgba > vbam > beetle-gba; gambatte > sameboy > mgba for GB/GBC), except lynx where handy is first because it boots without lynxboot.img, and dos where dosbox-pure is first for zip/gamepad support. Sega systems prefer genplus > picodrive > blastem (BlastEm's 32X/Mega-CD support is incomplete; genplus has no 32X). Arcade platforms map to fbneo only, which needs FBNeo romsets. extensions is the lowercase union of the listed cores' addon.xml extensions with the '/' directory marker dropped."
}
